## 2026-07-21 — Polish Pass Task 3: Arena wall collision skirt (slide-escape fix)

Playtest feedback: "you can slide out of the arena by just sliding into the
wall."

- Reproduced FIRST with a new headless harness (`test/TestArenaEscape.cs`):
  a scripted `CharacterBody3D` matching the player's slide capsule
  (Radius=0.35, Height=1.6 — confirmed the capsule is never resized during
  a slide, unlike the bug report's "shrinks the capsule" guess) driven at
  `SlideMaxEntry` (32 m/s) into the arena wall at several angles. A
  perpendicular hit on a plain wall face tunnelled clean through
  (`maxRadial=283` after 8s, vs a 30.36 escape threshold); diagonal hits
  into a corner/jamb were reliably blocked.
- Diagnosis: `ArenaBuilder`'s wall/floor/arch meshes are flat,
  zero-thickness double-sided trimesh quads. A raycast confirmed the
  collider genuinely IS present where the capsule tunnelled through — this
  is high-speed sweep tunnelling through a zero-thickness plane, not a
  positional gap.
- Fix: `ArenaBuilder.AddWallSkirt` — a new collision-only `StaticBody3D`
  ring of `BoxShape3D` colliders (real volume, 2m tall, 0.8m thick,
  overlapping the floor by 0.25m) lining every wall face's interior
  surface, plus jamb caps at both open doorways, plus a cylindrical corner
  post at all 32 polygon vertices (found necessary during verification — a
  capsule aimed exactly at the box/box seam between a wall face and a
  jamb cap tunnelled through the wedge gap between two differently-oriented
  boxes; a rotation-agnostic cylinder there closes it regardless of the
  angle mismatch). Zero MeshInstance3D — existing wall trimesh/visuals
  untouched.
- Re-ran the harness after each iteration: all wall-approach scenarios now
  stay well under the escape threshold with stable (non-creeping) blocked
  positions; both doorways remain fully passable (straight-through capsule
  reaches outside cleanly). `dotnet build` clean, 0 warnings/errors.
